{Complete game played through the board UI, level-3 computer, unlimited time, casual/unrated, anonymous. No analysis panel, engine assistance, hints, or takebacks used during the game. Final UI confirmed White checkmate: Ambrose lost as Black. Original observations are my own. Additional comments explicitly labelled Postgame use the visible local SF 19 1MB NNUE analysis panel after the game ended.}
1. d4 d5 2. e3 Nf6 3. h3 Bf5 4. Nf3 e6 5. c4 Bb4+
6. Bd2 Bxd2+ 7. Nbxd2 O-O 8. Be2 Nbd7 9. Qb3 Rb8
10. Qa4 Nb6 11. Qxa7 Ra8 12. Qxb7 Rb8 13. Qa7 Nxc4
14. Nb3 Nxb2 15. Ne5 Nc4 16. Bxc4 dxc4 17. Nc6 Ra8
18. Qb7 Qc8 19. Qxc8 Raxc8 20. Nc5 Rfe8 21. Ne5 c3
22. Rc1 c2 23. g4 Bg6 24. h4 h6 25. Nxg6 fxg6
26. Rxc2 e5 27. g5 Nd5 28. Rd2 exd4 29. gxh6 dxe3
{I focused on the pawn attacking Rd2 and missed that the rook could escape by capturing Nd5.}
{Postgame: before 29...dxe3, local evaluation +0.1 at depth 36; after it, +4.0 at depth 26, White perspective. The d4 pawn had blocked the white rook from Nd5.}
(29... Re5 {Postgame engine suggestion, manually tried on the analysis board: +0.2 at depth 35. Keeps the d4 blocker and directly protects Nd5. Only this move was played in this branch; no full continuation tested.})
30. Rxd5 e2 31. Rd2 Rb8 32. h7+ Kxh7 33. Nb3 Re4
34. f3 Re3 35. Rxe2 Rxe2+ 36. Kxe2 Ra8 37. Ra1 Ra4
38. Nc5 Rxh4 39. Ke3 Kh6 40. Ne6 c6 41. Rg1 Ra4
{Ra4 pursued the a-pawn but abandoned the h-file. My king's other exits were occupied by its own pawns or controlled by Ne6.}
(41... Kh7 {Postgame engine suggestion, manually tried: +5.9 at depth 32, White perspective. Avoids the immediate game continuation but remains substantially worse; not evidence of a draw. Only this alternative move was played.})
42. Rh1+ Rh4 43. Rxh4# 1-0


